---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';

const repo = 'https://github.com/atarik23/vae-mnist-digit-generation';
const figures = 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/atarik23/vae-mnist-digit-generation/main/figures';
const models = [
  { name: 'Autoencoder', architecture: 'Fully connected', latent: 32, mse: '0.00870' },
  { name: 'VAE', architecture: 'Fully connected', latent: 2, mse: '0.03982' },
  { name: 'VAE', architecture: 'Fully connected', latent: 16, mse: '0.01758' },
  { name: 'ConvVAE', architecture: 'Convolutional', latent: 16, mse: '0.01234' },
];
---

<Layout title="Variational Autoencoders for Handwritten Digit Generation — Tarik Agić">
  <main class="article">
    <a class="back" href="/work">← All projects</a>

    <header class="article-header">
      <p class="eyebrow">Machine Learning <span>·</span> Academic Project <span>·</span> 2026</p>
      <h1>Variational Autoencoders for Handwritten Digit Generation</h1>
      <p class="dek">An experimental comparison of autoencoder architectures for MNIST reconstruction, generation, and latent-space analysis.</p>
      <div class="byline">
        <span>Tarik Agić</span>
        <span class="separator" aria-hidden="true">·</span>
        <span>Individual project</span>
      </div>
      <nav class="resources" aria-label="Project resources">
        <a href={repo} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub ↗</a>
        <a href={`${repo}/blob/main/paper/seminar_paper.pdf`} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Full seminar paper ↗</a>
      </nav>
    </header>

    <article class="body">
      <section aria-labelledby="overview">
        <h2 id="overview">Overview</h2>
        <p>Developed for the <em>Machine Learning: Unsupervised Techniques</em> course at the Faculty of Electrical Engineering, University of Sarajevo, this project compares four autoencoder-based models trained on MNIST handwritten digits: a standard autoencoder, fully connected VAEs with 2- and 16-dimensional latent spaces, and a convolutional VAE with a 16-dimensional latent space.</p>
        <p>The experiments investigate reconstruction quality, random digit generation, interpolation, and the structure of learned latent representations.</p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="methodology">
        <h2 id="methodology">Methodology</h2>
        <p>All models were implemented in <strong>Python and PyTorch</strong> and trained on 28 × 28 grayscale MNIST images. The deterministic autoencoder minimizes mean squared error (MSE). The VAE models use the reparameterization trick and optimize binary cross-entropy reconstruction loss together with KL divergence.</p>
        <p>Models were trained for <strong>10 epochs</strong> with Adam (learning rate 0.001, batch size 128). Evaluation uses test-set reconstruction MSE; PCA and t-SNE support analysis of higher-dimensional latent spaces. Generated digits were assessed qualitatively rather than through a separate numerical generative-quality metric.</p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="results">
        <h2 id="results">Results</h2>
        <p>The standard autoencoder achieved the lowest reconstruction error. Among the VAE configurations, the convolutional model performed best on test-set MSE, while the 2D VAE offered a directly visualizable latent space at the cost of reconstruction accuracy.</p>
        <div class="table-scroll">
          <table>
            <caption>Reconstruction error on the MNIST test set (lower is better)</caption>
            <thead><tr><th scope="col">Model</th><th scope="col">Architecture</th><th scope="col">Latent dim.</th><th scope="col">MSE / pixel ↓</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
              {models.map((model) => <tr><td>{model.name}</td><td>{model.architecture}</td><td>{model.latent}</td><td class="numeric">{model.mse}</td></tr>)}
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <div class="figures">
          <figure>
            <img src={`${figures}/conv_vae_latent16_generated_digits.png`} alt="Grid of handwritten digits generated by the convolutional VAE" loading="lazy" />
            <figcaption><strong>Figure 1.</strong> Digits generated by sampling the convolutional VAE's latent space.</figcaption>
          </figure>
          <figure>
            <img src={`${figures}/conv_vae_latent16_interpolation_1_to_7.png`} alt="Sequence of generated handwritten digits interpolating between one and seven" loading="lazy" />
            <figcaption><strong>Figure 2.</strong> Interpolation between latent representations of handwritten digits.</figcaption>
          </figure>
        </div>
        <p>The results illustrate the trade-off between reconstruction accuracy and a regularized latent space suitable for sampling and interpolation. Additional plots, latent-space visualizations, and loss comparisons are available in the <a href={`${repo}/tree/main/figures`} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">repository figures ↗</a> and the <a href={`${repo}/blob/main/paper/seminar_paper.pdf`} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">full paper ↗</a>.</p>
      </section>
    </article>

    <footer class="article-footer">
      <span>Python · PyTorch · Torchvision · scikit-learn</span>
      <a href="/work">← Back to work</a>
    </footer>
  </main>
</Layout>

